					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2315616#post-2848929</guid>
				<title>Christmas is coming a little earlier than usual this year</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2315616/the-scp-173-christmas-eve-spectacular#post-2848929</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 10 Jun 2017 23:18:11 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Ba55</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3134834</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>SCP-173; a fixture in modern creepy internet stories that took the world by storm. It's ominous atmosphere left those who read it back in the day with a shiver down their backs and a craving for more. Many of the stories created for the contest attempt to capture the original horror of 173 using new and interesting angles not many have considered about this statue.</p> <p>And then there's this one, which is just plain stupid.</p> <p>To throw my hat into the ring, here's a nice, innocent Christmas tale that involves SCP-173. What could possibly go wrong?</p> <p>Anyways, I tried to make you chuckle at least. So; if I did that, I'll be happy.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
